body:
#### PR description:

Histogram ranges of the BTV DQM/validation adjusted where entries fall outside. Follows #52368 and #52463. Rule: a range is changed only if more than 2 % of the entries are outside it in one of the RelVals:
- 17_0_0_pre3: BTagMu data, QCD, TTbar PU;
- 20_1_0_pre2: TTbar and QCD Pt15To7000 Flat 2026 PU, BTagMu 2025E, Phase-2 TTbar D121 PU200;
- any flavour, histograms with >= 200 entries.

One range for Run 3 and Phase-2; bin widths kept where possible. Details and numbers per histogram are in the commit messages.
- **TagInfo features (UParT, ParticleNet Forward, `MiniAODTagInfoAnalyzer`):**
  - include weight/fraction = 1 (was in the overflow);
  - book signed features and default values in range;
  - widen impact parameter, significance and SV ranges;
  - zoom in on narrow features;
  - variable bins (new `book1DVariable()`) for heavy tails.
- **AOD IPTag (`IPTagPlotter`, `tagGenericAnalysis_cff.py`):** widen only the 17 IP value/significance histograms that overflow. They get their own range through the new `WideRangeHistograms` parameter, with the same bin width. Also widened: `tkPt*`, `tkNPixelHits*` (Phase-2), `ghostTrackDistSign`, `selTrksNbr`, and the `(selected)TrackMultVsJetPt` axes. The jet pT axis goes up to 7 TeV, as `jetPt_extended` (#52368).
- **BDHadronTracks validation:** ranges chosen per track category (PU, BWeakDecay, ...). The harvested `nTrk_absolute/relative/std_*`, which ignore the overflow, change for nTrkAll and Other.

No histogram is added or removed. Only binning/ranges change, so mean, RMS and over/underflow of the affected histograms change in RelMon, and the cms-bot DQM comparison will count these histograms as changed.

#### PR validation:

`scram b` without warnings, `code-checks` and `code-format` without changes. runTheMatrix steps 3+4 of wf 16834.0 (Run 3 2025) and 29634.0 (Phase-2 D110), 100 events, compared with master: all steps exit 0, same histogram list, only the IPTag, TagInfo and BDHadronTracks histograms listed above change. Full 20_1_0_pre2 RelVals (TTbar, QCD, BTagMu 2025E, Phase-2 TTbar, DQM steps 3+4) with these changes on top of #52463: all histograms below 2 % outside except the cases explained in the commit messages, no NaN, efficiencies in [0, 1]. Data: T0 PromptReco config (`RunPromptReco.py`, ppEra_Run3_2024, BTagMu Run2024I RAW, 1000 events): exit 0, changes only in IPTag/TagInfo ranges.


